# War of Princes — Setting & Premise

*A Vampire: The Dark Ages chronicle. London and the Baronies of Avalon, 1242, under the domain of Mithras.*

> This file is narrative flavor for the chronicle. The mechanical house rules live alongside it in
> `vtm5e-war-of-princes-character-creation.ttrpg` and `vtm5e-war-of-princes-roads.ttrpg`.

## Our Story

The year is 1242. The War of Princes engulfs Europe and beyond. The meticulous game of the Long Night
has given way to an escalation of violence among the Cainites. The destruction of mighty empires has
awakened a sense of desperation and paranoia among many Elders. Others seek to exploit the
opportunities birthed by the chaos.

As wars rage across battlefields, in palace courts, and within the shadows, our coterie receives a task
to take them across the Baronies of Avalon and beyond. Their choices may tip the scales of power across
Cainite society — or leave them the latest victims of the endless violence.

## Lore & Liberties

The Dark Ages book is shared for reference, but its lore is not authoritative for our game. We aim for
some historical accuracy while taking liberties with Vampire lore, so we are not retelling established
tales but forging our own narrative. Some NPCs may be recognizable, others brand new — all molded to
best serve our shared story.

This is **before** the Inquisition, the formation of the sects, and the Beckoning. Most danger comes
from regional or political conflicts, personal strife, and greater horrors that lurk in the lands
between protected domains.

## The World in 1242

- **Mithras** rules the Baronies of Avalon from his seat in London — a powerful elder who has
  cultivated a godlike mythology.
- **The Rose Treaty** was recently established to end a revolt of the Baronies, recognizing their
  domains and granting Barons representation on Mithras's council. Great tension remains between many
  Baronies and Mithras; hostilities between the **Tremere** and Mithras are especially volatile.
- Other major governing powers: **The Courts of Love** (France), the **Fiefs of the Black Cross** (the
  Holy Roman Empire), the **Sea of Shadows** (the Iberian Peninsula), the **Voivodate** (the Carpathian
  Mountains), the **Italian City States**, and **The Ashirra** (Arabia and North Africa). Most are
  currently embroiled in some form of active conflict.
- **Caine** is widely accepted as the progenitor of vampires.
- It is common for Kindred to practice a major religion such as Christianity or Islam.
- Elder vampires exert near-absolute control over younger Cainites in most domains.
- **Clan** plays a major part in most Cainites' lives, establishing their place in society and defining
  their enemies. Tension and mistrust among certain clans is key to the political horror of the Dark
  Ages.
- Most domains follow the **Traditions of Caine**. Mithras enforces his **Blood Laws**, which remove
  worship of Caine (the Covenant) as a rule. *(The Traditions and clan availability are enumerated
  mechanically in the character-creation file.)*

## The Coterie

You are a London-based coterie trusted as an **envoy** for Kindred of moderate status. Given the perils
of travel at this time, this is a dangerous position — but one that comes with rare opportunities for
those who survive.

You may be in the coterie by choice, assigned for your skillset, pressured into it by an elder, or any
number of reasons. While ultimately under the authority of Mithras, the coterie answers to various
influential Cainites in need of its services. The work ranges from important diplomatic representation
to simply delivering or receiving messages.

The chronicle begins with the coterie on the way back to London after a simple task: picking up an
unknown package from Norway. How long the current iteration of the coterie has been together is up to
the party, to be fleshed out at Session Zero.

Loyalties will be tested and ambitions challenged, but the coterie should ultimately intend to work
together toward a common goal. Tension between characters is welcome; constant inner-coterie turmoil is
not — there will be plenty of antagonists more rewarding to engage with.

## Session Zero

We finalize character concepts, build character connections, discuss safety tools, and answer any
questions about the chronicle. It is scheduled on StartPlaying, but you will not be charged for it.
